# MedShadow Authentication System

## Overview
This document outlines the authentication system implementation for MedShadow, a platform connecting students with medical shadowing opportunities.

## Core Authentication Components

### 1. NextAuth Configuration
- Main configuration file: [src/app/api/auth/[...nextauth]/authOptions.ts](mdc:src/app/api/auth/[...nextauth]/authOptions.ts)
- Route handler: [src/app/api/auth/[...nextauth]/route.ts](mdc:src/app/api/auth/[...nextauth]/route.ts)
- Authentication providers:
  - Email/Password (Credentials)
  - Google OAuth

### 2. User Model & Types
- Location: [src/models/User.ts](mdc:src/models/User.ts)
- Required fields:
  - name (String)
  - email (String, unique)
  - password (String, hashed)
  - role (enum: student/facility)
- Optional fields:
  - education
  - skills
  - interests
  - facilityInfo
- TypeScript types: [user.ts](mdc:src/types/user.ts)
  - UserRole enum (STUDENT, FACILITY)
  - Base user interface
  - Education and facility information types

### 3. Authentication UI Components
- [SignUpForm.tsx](mdc:src/components/auth/SignUpForm.tsx)
  - Handles new user registration
  - Supports both email/password and Google OAuth
  - Validates passwords and enforces requirements
  - Integrates with UserRole enum for role selection
- [SignInForm.tsx](mdc:src/components/auth/SignInForm.tsx)
  - Manages user login
  - Supports email/password and Google authentication
  - Handles callback URLs for redirects
  - Stores JWT token in localStorage
- [NavbarUserDropdown.tsx](mdc:src/components/layout/NavbarUserDropdown.tsx)
  - Displays user info and sign out option

### 4. Protected Routes
- Middleware: [src/middleware.ts](mdc:src/middleware.ts)
- Public routes:
  - /
  - /auth/signin
  - /auth/signup
- Protected routes:
  - /dashboard/*
  - /applications/*
  - /opportunities/*
  - /profile/*

## Implementation Guidelines

### 1. Authentication Flow
1. User attempts to access protected route
2. Middleware checks for valid session
3. If no session:
   - Redirect to signin with callback URL
4. If session exists:
   - Verify role-based access
   - Allow/deny access accordingly

### 2. Session Management
- JWT-based sessions
- 30-day session duration
- 24-hour session update interval
- Automatic token refresh

### 3. Security Requirements
- Password requirements:
  - Minimum 8 characters
  - At least one uppercase letter
  - At least one lowercase letter
  - At least one number
  - At least one special character
- Rate limiting:
  - 5 attempts per 15 minutes for login
  - 3 attempts per hour for password reset
- CSRF protection on all forms
- Email verification required for new accounts

### 4. Role-Based Access Control
- Student access:
  - Dashboard
  - Applications
  - Profile
  - Resources
- Facility access:
  - Dashboard
  - Opportunities
  - Profile
  - Applications management

### 5. Error Handling
- Standardized error responses
- User-friendly error messages
- Secure error logging
- Rate limit exceeded handling
- Invalid credentials handling
- Session expired handling

### 6. UI & Styling Best Practices
- Always use the UserRole enum for role management
- Include proper type checking for user objects
- Handle loading and error states in forms
- Use the built-in password hashing in the User model
- Use established styling patterns:
  - `form-input` for inputs
  - `btn-primary` for main actions
  - `btn-secondary` for alternative actions
  - Consistent error message styling

